hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18994","Bahz and Abu Kamil narrated to us, they said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated, Simak narrated to us, from Alqamah ibn Wail, from Tariq ibn Suwayd al-Hadrami, that he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, in our land are grapes we press and drink from. He said: No. So I repeated to him, and he said: No. So I said: We seek cure with it for the sick. So he said: That is not a cure, but it is a disease."
"18995","Hajjaj ibn Muhammad and Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, they said: Shubah narrated, from Simak ibn Harb, from Alqamah ibn Wail, from his father Wail ibn Hujr al-Hadrami, Hajjaj said: He witnessed the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and a man from Khatham called Suwayd ibn Tariq asked him, and Ibn Jafar said: or Tariq ibn Suwayd al-Jufi asked the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about wine, so he forbade him, then he mentioned the hadith."
"22869","Abu Kamil narrated to us: Hammad narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Alqamah ibn Wail, from Tariq ibn Suwayd al-Hadrami, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, indeed in our land are grapes we press; shall we drink from it? He said: No. So I returned to him, and he said: No. Then I returned to him, and he said: No. So I said: Indeed we seek healing with it for the sick. He said: Indeed it is not a healing, but it is a disease."
